**Owner:** Worf (commissioner); Rom (executor)
**Why:** The launchd-managed orchestrator inherits a minimal `PATH` from `launchd` that excludes `/usr/local/bin` (where `claude` is installed). Result: `claude -p` spawn returns `ENOENT, durationMs: 3` immediately. Slice 299 (May 9) worked because that orchestrator was nohup-launched from Philipp's shell which had a full PATH; after the May 13 launchctl reload, the daemon lost it. Bit slice 294's May 14 dispatch attempt; will bite every future dispatch the same way.

---

## Goal

Add a `PATH` key to `scripts/dev.liberation.orchestrator.plist`'s `EnvironmentVariables` dict so the launchd-spawned orchestrator can resolve `claude`, `node` (via nvm), and standard system binaries.

Mechanical plist edit. One key addition.

---

## Scope

### Change

`scripts/dev.liberation.orchestrator.plist` — modify the `EnvironmentVariables` dict to add:

```xml
<key>PATH</key>
<string>/usr/local/bin:/Users/phillyvanilly/.nvm/versions/node/v24.11.1/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
```

Result should be:

```xml
<key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
<dict>
    <key>HOME</key>
    <string>/Users/phillyvanilly</string>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/usr/local/bin:/Users/phillyvanilly/.nvm/versions/node/v24.11.1/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
</dict>
```

Use `plistlib` via `python3` for safe XML edit, or hand-edit if the indentation matches. Don't reorder existing keys; just add the PATH key alongside HOME.

### Verify

After the edit:
1. `python3 -c "import plistlib; print(plistlib.load(open('scripts/dev.liberation.orchestrator.plist','rb'))['EnvironmentVariables']['PATH'])"` outputs the expected PATH string.
2. `plutil -lint scripts/dev.liberation.orchestrator.plist` returns "OK".
3. The plist's other keys (Label, ProgramArguments, WorkingDirectory, KeepAlive, etc.) are unchanged. Diff should show ONLY the PATH addition.

---

## Out of scope

- Reloading the launchd agent (`launchctl unload && launchctl load`). Rom can't run launchctl from `claude -p`. Philipp or the orchestrator runbook handles activation. Note in the DONE report that activation is separately needed.
- Refactoring the plist beyond the PATH addition.
- Touching `scripts/orch-start.sh` or any other startup helper.

---

## Acceptance criteria

| # | Criterion |
|---|---|
| 1 | `plutil -lint` returns "OK" on the modified plist. |
| 2 | `EnvironmentVariables.PATH` contains `/usr/local/bin` and the nvm node bin dir. |
| 3 | All other keys (Label, ProgramArguments, WorkingDirectory, KeepAlive, ThrottleInterval, StandardOutPath, StandardErrorPath, HOME) unchanged. |
| 4 | DONE report notes that `launchctl unload && launchctl load` is required separately to activate. |
| 5 | Backup of original plist exists at `scripts/dev.liberation.orchestrator.plist.bak-<ts>` (or equivalent). |

